WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.560
Avengers: Endgame may very well be the last
time we see Thanos as a villain in the Marvel

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.820
Cinematic Universe.

00:00:06.029 --> 00:00:10.100
And though the comics have plenty of bad guys
to choose from, filling Thanos' shoes won't

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:10.680
be easy.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:14.080
It's got to be someone truly powerful and
truly scary.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:18.860
Here's a look at some of the villains who
could be the next MCU big bad after Thanos.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:23.880
In Marvel lore, the Celestials are a race
of cosmic beings who created intelligent life

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.620
forms across the galaxy — including humanity
— as a grand experiment.

00:00:27.820 --> 00:00:32.160
And when that experiment fails to meet their
standards, the Celestials… end it.

00:00:32.170 --> 00:00:35.920
They've already shown up in Guardians of the
Galaxy, with one of their heads serving as

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.100
the outpost called Knowhere, and they’re
rumored to possibly be in the upcoming Eternals

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:45.020
movie, meaning the heroes of the MCU could
literally meet their makers sooner rather

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:45.700
than later.

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:50.640
Of the villains we've actually seen in the
MCU, possibly the most staggeringly powerful

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.120
was the godlike Dormammu of 2016's Doctor
Strange.

00:00:54.320 --> 00:00:59.900
Even Stephen Strange himself realized he had
no prayer of defeating Dormammu, so he resorted

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:03.940
to some clever trickery to get the entity
to promise not to mess with Earth again.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:08.640
But oaths are made to be broken, and if Dormammu
returns, it might take the combined might

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:10.640
of all the MCU heroes to stop him.

00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:15.080
One of the better kept secrets of Infinity
War was the surprise reappearance of Captain

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.470
America's old enemy, the Red Skull.

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:22.790
Audiences hadn't seen him on the big screen
since 2011's Captain America: The First Avenger,

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:26.480
and the crimson-faced Hydra-founder's fate
had been something of a mystery.

00:01:26.760 --> 00:01:30.660
With Thanos gone, though, Red Skull may finally
be free to return to Earth.

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:33.900
And who knows how his experience in space
has changed him?

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.740
The dude was dangerous enough even before
being cursed by an Infinity Stone.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:38.600
Now?

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:40.440
He might even be a match for the Avengers.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:45.580
Ever since fans learned that the shapeshifting
alien Skrulls were going to appear in Captain

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:51.260
Marvel, there's been speculation about a big
screen version of Secret Invasion, the 2008

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:55.920
Marvel Comics event that revealed the shapeshifting
aliens had been infiltrating the Earth for

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:56.420
years.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:02:02.200
Or maybe the groundbreaking 1971 epic Kree-Skrull
War, which was at the heart of Captain Marvel.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:04.920
Sure, the Skrulls in that film turned out
to be okay.

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:08.590
But there could be plenty more that may not
be quite so nice, meaning either of these

00:02:08.590 --> 00:02:11.820
epic storylines could still be in store for
MCU fans.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:17.000
When a Marvel Comics reader thinks big, cosmic,
world-threatening villain, Galactus is probably

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.400
the first one to come to mind.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:23.450
An immortal entity who has lived since before
the Big Bang, Galactus must feed his insatiable

00:02:23.450 --> 00:02:25.680
hunger by devouring entire planets whole.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:30.960
He sort of made an appearance in 2007's Fantastic
4: Rise of the Silver Surfer.

00:02:31.340 --> 00:02:33.620
But not really, as he was just a goofy cloud.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:38.400
Now that Disney has re-acquired the rights
to Galactus from 20th Century Fox, a glimpse

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:41.540
of his classic outfit and hearing some booming
voice say "I…

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:44.700
HUNGER!" would be all you need to get fans
ready for Phase 4.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:48.500
How awesome would it be to see the Avengers
fight the Justice League?

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:52.820
Well, it's not as crazy as you think, because
Marvel actually has their own version of the

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:53.740
Justice League.

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:58.680
Called The Squadron Supreme, this alternate
universe group of heroes features characters

00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:01.960
that are all analogues of DC icons, like Superman...

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:02.960
Wonder Woman...

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:03.960
Green Lantern...

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:05.220
Flash... and Aquaman.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:09.819
Sure, it would be a cheeky surprise if Marvel
decided to risk a lawsuit from Warner Bros.

00:03:09.820 --> 00:03:12.020
by promoting the Squadron to star players.

00:03:12.340 --> 00:03:14.080
But comic book fans would be over the moon.

00:03:14.200 --> 00:03:16.200
The payoff might just be worth the risk.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:21.180
It isn't clear whether or not Mark Ruffalo
will be continuing to appear as the Hulk after

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:22.220
Avengers: Endgame.

00:03:22.580 --> 00:03:26.020
But if he does, there's an intriguing option
on the table: Maestro.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:30.400
It's been rumored for awhile that Bruce Banner
and Hulk may reconcile their differences from

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:35.420
Avengers: Infinity War by combining into Professor
Hulk, a version of the character who has the

00:03:35.420 --> 00:03:38.120
Hulk's brute strength but Banner's brilliant
mind.

00:03:38.680 --> 00:03:41.580
Now imagine what might happen if someone like
that turned evil?

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:46.560
That's the idea behind Maestro, who in the
comics is a future version of Hulk who has

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:50.120
taken over the world and murdered all the
other heroes in the process.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:52.140
Now there's a threat that's truly chilling.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:56.260
When it comes to Avengers villains, though,
there's one that stands out above all the

00:03:56.260 --> 00:04:01.340
rest — above Loki, above Ultron, and even
above Thanos: Kang the Conqueror.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:05.800
In the comics, no villain has more consistently
given the Avengers more trouble than Kang,

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:10.920
a warlord from the distant future who uses
time travel to invade other eras with his

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:13.060
technologically superior armies.

00:04:13.209 --> 00:04:17.600
Kang is another character whose rights had
been tied up at 20th Century Fox, but now

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:21.870
that Avengers: Endgame is rumored to involve
time travel, it seems like the time might

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.820
finally be right for Kang to make his long
awaited appearance.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:29.680
Arguably Marvel's most important villain in
the comics, Doctor Doom has appeared in two

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:35.050
different Fox iterations of the Fantastic
Four movie franchise...and both versions have

00:04:35.050 --> 00:04:37.200
been, for lack of a better term, total poop.

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:41.720
But like Galactus, Marvel Studios now has
the movie rights to the character, so they

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:42.800
can do the doom right.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:46.880
Doctor Doom has the presence and the power
to give anyone a run for their money: not

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:51.620
only is he basically an evil Tony Stark, with
genius level intellect and a suit of super

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:55.180
armor to match, he's also a sorcerer who can
hang with Doctor Strange.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:58.740
And you know what can happen when more than
one powerful doctor gets in the same room

00:04:58.740 --> 00:04:59.240
together...

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:05.800
"...I don't have to say anything.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.200
I'm a doctor too."

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:12.240
And those aren't the only heroes for whom
Doctor Doom is an evil reflection.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:16.660
Think seeing a big screen version of Wakanda,
ruled by the heroic Black Panther, was amazing?

00:05:16.660 --> 00:05:21.580
Imagine how awesome it'd be to see an MCU
version of Doctor Doom ruling Latveria with

00:05:21.580 --> 00:05:22.920
a literal iron fist.

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:27.610
In the comics, he's beaten the Avengers and
taken over the world single-handedly, so we

00:05:27.610 --> 00:05:30.540
can't wait to see him in the MCU sooner or
later.

